# WalkQuest Project Rules

# Design system (Material 3 Expressive)
- Colours come from generated tokens (npm run theme); never hard-code hex colours in components
- Use var(--md-sys-color-*) directly (tokens are real colours); for transparency use color-mix(), not rgb(var())
- Prefer the Tailwind theme utilities (bg-surface-container-low, text-on-surface, rounded-m3-lg, type-title-medium, state-layer, shape-morph)
- Build UI from components/m3/* (M3Button, M3IconButton, M3Chip, M3Menu, M3FabMenu, M3BottomSheet, M3LoadingIndicator)
- Icons: material-symbols:*-rounded via <Icon>; run npm run icons (build does it) to bundle new ones

# Frontend patterns
- Vue 3 Composition API (<script setup>); Pinia for shared state
- Large collections live in shallowRef/frozen objects; never deep-proxy the walk index
- One filter pipeline: stores/searchStore.js (pure logic in utils/walks.js); list and map both consume it
- css/app.css is the only global stylesheet; component styles are scoped

# Walk list
- Load every walk at once from /api/walks (ETag-cached, IndexedDB copy); no pagination
- Virtualise with RecycleScroller and a fixed item size (120px)
- Fetch details/geometry on demand via the walks store / services/api.js

# Map
- Raw mapbox-gl in components/map/WalkMap.vue; no DOM markers and no clustering
- All walks are one GeoJSON source; hover/selection via feature-state; build layers in utils/mapLayers.js
- Zoom expressions must be the top-level interpolate/step input
- Clean up map listeners/observers in onBeforeUnmount

# Motion
- CSS: --md-sys-motion-spring-* tokens; JS: springs from js/design/motion.js with motion's animate({ ease | type: 'spring' })
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion

# Development flow
- Frontend: npm test and npm run build; Backend: ruff, manage.py check, makemigrations --check, pytest
- New features need tests (Vitest for pure JS, pytest for API/commands)
